# DO nancy-drew.rosetta-fixes --into=<the game's folder> --exe=<its program's file name>
#
# Makes the game run at speed under Rosetta, whose software x87 maths made a
# scene with sounds and snow playing drop to a frame every couple of seconds:
# its Ogg Vorbis decoding is replaced by one built for SSE2, and its particle
# system's catch-up after a slow frame is capped. Both are done by a proxy
# comdlg32.dll in the game's folder, which the game is made to load before
# Wine's own (and which passes every comdlg32 call on to it). A game whose
# code it doesn't recognise is left as it is. Built from
# Packages/Modules/nancy-drew/RosettaFixes; docs/modules.md#rosetta-fixes.
FUNCTION rosetta-fixes
  INPUT into
  INPUT exe
  COPY assets/rosetta-fixes/comdlg32.dll ${input.into}/comdlg32.dll
  WINE.REGISTRY --set "HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Wine\AppDefaults\${input.exe}\DllOverrides:comdlg32" native,builtin
END
